{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/kzaxgn2h","slide":2,"text":"A model is one component—not the decision-maker.","textPreview":"A model is one component—not the decision-maker.","textChars":48,"textLines":1,"bbox":[58,530,560,52]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/nvrqgo","slide":2,"text":"The central idea is simple. Quality requires outcomes, safety, experience, equity, and continuity. The five controls shown here are Outcomes, Safety, Experience, Equity, Continuity. Together, they prevent a health signal from being mistaken for an authorized decision.\n\n[Sources]\n- Canonical notebook V7_B_N11, SRAI Book 7 v1.0."}
